 "transcript": {
  "answer": "I can't give you an AUD/ARS rate. The RBA exchange-rate tables I have access to don't include the Argentine peso. They cover USD, EUR, JPY, GBP, CNY, NZD and a few others, but not ARS. I'd rather not guess, because the peso's official and market rates can differ a lot and move quickly.\n\nThe latest figure I do have is A$1 = US$0.6947 (RBA, 4pm AEST, 16 October 2026). To get pesos, multiply that by the current USD/ARS rate. For example, if USD/ARS were 1,000, A$1 would be about 695 pesos. That 1,000 is only an illustration, not a real quote. For a live figure, check a currency converter or the Banco de la Nación Argentina. Note that Argentina can have both an official rate and a parallel market rate.",
